  "published": "2025-09-25T07:27:27.733Z",
  "releaseNotes": "## [4.8.2.0] - 2025-09-15\n\n### Fixed\n\n- An issue where the SDK would throw a NACK exception with TRANSMIT_FAILED when sending a GNP packet to a child device that was removed while sending. \n  TRANSMIT_FAILED is always a sign that the child device has disconnected. The SDK now throws a DeviceDisconnectedException in this case.\n\n- An regression was introduced in the Device Connector for Windows version 2.0.0 where softphone focus events were formatted incorrectly. \n  The .NET SDK used the same incorrect format and was not subject to the issue. \n  This has now been fixed in the Device Connector for Windows version 2.2.10 to align with other Device Connectors and SDKs. The .NET SDK has also been updated to use the same format.\n\n- An issue where the SDK would not prioritize Bluetooth LE over Bluetooth Classic when both connections were available. If both connections are available, Bluetooth LE will now be prioritized.  \n\n- An issue where rejecting an incoming call in Easy Call Control would cause the app to crash. This could happen if there were no incoming calls when calling the method to reject an incoming call.",
